  "source_review": [
    "Each outstanding frame owns one block and one pool reference; decoder owner holds a distinct reference.",
    "Only returned blocks enter the mutex-protected idle list; at most two idle blocks per decoder, exact-size reuse, 64-byte output alignment.",
    "Cached blocks own no references, avoiding an ownership cycle. Close marks the pool closed, detaches and frees idle blocks, then drops only the decoder reference.",
    "Concurrent frame return versus close is safe: the returning frame keeps the pool alive and never touches a cached block after unlock; only the last atomic reference clears the mutex and frees the pool.",
    "Decoder calls remain externally serialized. The broker hardware mutex provides that serialization while frame_free may happen after unlock and network send.",
    "The broker releases every delivered frame through cedar_frame_free including send failures; no caller free(data) was found.",
    "Output pixels, dimensions, timestamps, crop checks, memcpy path, DMA allocator and hardware lifecycle are unchanged."
  ],
